WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
I'll give the coding agent a focused task.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.920
Fix the invoice search vulnerability
while preserving normal search behavior.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.480
We'll choose the repository and branch,

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.220
select plan mode and review the
approach before implementation.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:17.520
As the agent works, I'll follow
its progress and add a test case.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.100
Then we'll inspect the patch
and validation and open

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.620
a pull request so the team
can review the result.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.180
I open a coding task and
select the repository

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.400
and branch containing our
invoice search feature.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.200
The problem is that search text is
inserted directly into a database command.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.140
A crafted search could change that command

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.120
and retrieve another customer's invoices.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.660
My request describes the result we need.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.320
Keep search results within the customer's
account and treat search text as data.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.940
I also describe the behavior to preserve.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:54.020
Customers should still be able
to search using part of a product

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.000
name and results should keep
their existing order and limit.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.300
I ask for regression tests
that demonstrate the fix.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.340
This task covers invoice
search and its tests with the

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.480
discount and invoice export
issues left for separate work.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:10.520
Before implementation, I
want to review the approach.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.020
I open the mode menu beside the
task description and select plan.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.040
The label confirms that choice
before I send the request.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:21.640
The agent reads the repository
and proposes an approach.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.080
I open the plan to check what it intends

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.460
to change and how it will test the result.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:31.660
It proposes separating the search
values from the SQL command,

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.980
then checking both ordinary searches and
attempts to cross the customer boundary.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.830
I compare that with my request.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.920
The plan needs to preserve useful search

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.380
behavior as well as
address the vulnerability.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.620
At the end, the agent asks
whether to implement the plan.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.760
I can request changes here if
the scope or approach needs work.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.200
For this task, I select
yes, implement this plan.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.480
That starts the implementation
in the task workspace.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.960
We'll inspect the finished
patch before publishing it.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.400
I open the task activity
to follow the agent as

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.120
it reads files, edits the
code, and runs commands.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.380
The workspace keeps the implementation

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.660
available for inspection
while the agent works.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.580
These edits haven't yet
been published to GitHub.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.500
I add a specific test request.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.800
Check a product name containing
an apostrophe and check that

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.600
another customer's matching
invoice stays out of the result.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.600
Those are useful cases because
the fix needs to preserve

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.840
ordinary text searches while
maintaining the customer boundary.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.660
When the task finishes,
I read the response.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.380
The agent confirms that both cases passed.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:39.480
It also reports the overall test
results and dependency audit.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.740
The optional CodeRabbit review was
disabled for this task, so it didn't run.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.320
I'll keep that in mind as I open the
patch and inspect the validation myself.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.280
I open the changed files and start
with the invoice search query.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:55.900
The SQL command now uses placeholders.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.130
The customer account and search
text are supplied separately,

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.100
allowing the database
to treat them as values.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.560
Next, I open the regression tests.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.400
The test for the original security problem

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.680
is now a normal assertion that must pass.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.840
It checks that a crafted search cannot
retrieve another customer's invoices.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.920
I also inspect the ordinary cases.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.160
Partial name searches, a
product name with an apostrophe,

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.740
the expected result order,
and the result limit.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.780
The recorded task reports 76
passed tests and 4 unrelated

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.800
expected failures along with
a clean dependency audit.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.040
The additional CodeRabbit review didn't
run, as we saw in the task settings.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.780
If the patch missed the requirement, I
could ask the agent to revise it here.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.980
For this example, the
code and tests address the

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.240
requested behavior, so
I'll move to delivery.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.980
The task offers commit
and push or create PR.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.120
I choose create PR so the
fix can have its own review.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.760
That action starts publishing the change.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:58.860
Once it finishes, I follow the link to
GitHub and check the destination branch.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.660
This fix targets our
original feature branch,

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:05.720
keeping the invoice search correction
separate from the larger feature.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:10.200
I check that the pull request contains
the expected query change and tests.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.120
These are the changes we inspected in
the task, now available to the team.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.740
The delivery step didn't rerun validation.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.340
The earlier results are
recorded in the coding task.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.000
Automatic review was also skipped
for this feature branch destination.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.860
We've scoped the work,
reviewed a plan, followed the

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.600
implementation and inspected
the patch before delivery.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:34.320
The pull request remains
open for the team's review.
